\begin{abstract}
This note states the foundational publication principle of the CEUME / SIE-ASTRO
architecture: that all claims are subordinate to mathematically and physically
validated structures. Doubt is resolved not by opinion, but by direct reference
to conservation laws, invariant formulations, and stress-tested numerical
solvers.
\end{abstract}

\section{Foundational Principle}

The CEUME and SIE-ASTRO frameworks are constructed under the following axiom:

\medskip

\noindent\textbf{Axiom (Primacy of Consistency).}
Let $\mathcal{M}$ denote the mathematical model space and $\mathcal{P}$ the
physical law space (e.g.\ conservation laws, geodesic constraints, stress-energy
relations). A result $R$ is admissible in the framework if and only if
\[
R \in \mathcal{M} \cap \mathcal{P},
\]
i.e.\ it is simultaneously:
\begin{itemize}
    \item mathematically consistent (well-posed, convergent, invariant-respecting),
    \item physically consistent (compatible with established dynamics and constraints).
\end{itemize}

Any objection to $R$ must therefore be expressed as either:
\begin{enumerate}
    \item a demonstrated violation of $\mathcal{M}$ (e.g.\ non-convergence, algebraic inconsistency), or
    \item a demonstrated violation of $\mathcal{P}$ (e.g.\ broken conservation, invalid geodesic, non-physical state).
\end{enumerate}
Objections that do not explicitly reference $\mathcal{M}$ or $\mathcal{P}$ are
classified as non-technical and do not alter the status of $R$.

\section{Operational Interpretation}

In practice, this axiom is enforced via:
\begin{itemize}
    \item explicit conservation equations for relativistic MHD,
    \item null geodesic constraints in curved spacetimes,
    \item Dirac--Fock energy residual bounds,
    \item post-quantum cryptographic state verification.
\end{itemize}

Thus, disagreement with a CEUME / SIE-ASTRO result is, by construction,
disagreement with:
\begin{itemize}
    \item the equations solved,
    \item the physics encoded,
    \item or the proofs binding the states.
\end{itemize}
In all cases, resolution proceeds by examining the math and physics; once these
are verified, the result stands.

